    "summary": "A four-year-old accidentally broke a rare 3,500-year-old bronze age jar while visiting the Hecht Museum in Haifa, Israel with his mother. The jar, used to hold wine or oil, had been on display for 35 years before the incident. The family returned to the museum a week later, where the staff and curators welcomed them back warmly. The boy, Ariel, gifted the museum a clay vase of his own as a gesture of apology and forgiveness.",
    "keywords": ["break", "jar", "bronze age", "museum", "accident"]
}

